  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.087,
            0.889,
            0.123
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Set up a filtration apparatus and filter each mixture separately. Is there any residue left on the filter paper?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.125,
            0.89,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Based on your observations, do you think these are the same types of mixtures or are they different?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.236,
            0.209,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 8 Curiosity Chapter 9"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.163,
            0.888,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These are indeed different types of mixtures. How? Let us explore further!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.211,
            0.395,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.2 Solutions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.234,
            0.89,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have learnt that solutions are homogeneous mixtures. You have also learnt that solutions are prepared when a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "solute",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (the substance that gets dissolved) is mixed with a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "solvent",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (the substance that dissolves the solute). In the mixture of sugar and water, sugar is the solute, and water is the solvent. In what proportion are a solute and a solvent present in a solution? Can these be expressed quantitatively?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.375,
            0.208,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 6 Curiosity Chapter 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.346,
            0.59,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.2.1 Concentration of a solution"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.059,
            0.451,
            0.115,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.368,
            0.89,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have learnt how Oral Rehydration Solution (ORS) is prepared. We add specified amounts of salt and sugar to a fixed amount of water to prepare ORS. If we change the amount of salt or sugar added to the same volume of water, or change the volume of water for the specified amounts of salt and sugar, we will get a solution of salt and sugar in water, but that will not be ORS. In other words, we cannot freely add any amount of salt and sugar to a fixed amount of water to make ORS."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.474,
            0.196,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Not all sugary drinks prepared at home or sold in the market are ORS."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.49,
            0.89,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us take another example. When farmers spray pesticides on their crops, they must mix the right amount of pesticide with a fixed amount of water to prepare a solution. If they do not do so, what is likely to happen? Too little pesticide may not protect crops, while too much can damage crops, soil and the environment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.053,
            0.583,
            0.221,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Meet a Scientist"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.061,
            0.607,
            0.18,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.061,
                0.607,
                0.18,
                0.714
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.609,
            0.304,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Dilip Mahalanabis",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", an Indian paediatrician, first developed and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.361,
            0.578,
            0.712,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you think of other such examples?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.062,
            0.717,
            0.304,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "implemented the treatment for dehydration caused by diseases, such as diarrhoea and cholera. He formulated the ORS that has revolutionised rehydration therapy. It has saved millions of lives after the World Health Organization (WHO) popularised it worldwide."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.329,
            0.598,
            0.888,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The right proportion is always essential when preparing a solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.636,
            0.89,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The amount of solute dissolved in a given amount of solvent or solution is termed as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "concentration",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.329,
            0.689,
            0.89,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Understanding concentration is essential not only in science laboratories but also in everyday life, whether in medicine, agriculture, food, cosmetics, or even while making a simple cup of tea!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.331,
            0.768,
            0.78,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.2.2 How do we express concentration?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.79,
            0.889,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us now explore the different ways to express the concentration of a solution, and understand where and why each method is more suitable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.33,
            0.844,
            0.889,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Collect some commercial packaged products (Fig. 5.4) and note down the information given for each item."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.927,
            0.122,
            0.994
          ],
